<tools-used-before-summary>AskUserQuestion, Bash, Read</tools-used-before-summary>
Summary:
## 1. Primary Request and Intent

The user's opening request (accompanied by an attached PDF at `Documents/Canteen-APIs-for-HRMS-22-Oct.pdf`):

> "So based on this @Documents/Canteen-APIs-for-HRMS-22-Oct.pdf you have made me APIs. We need to display them properly on our UI as well. THis does have a mobile app version but also we need to have FE UI! Can you help make the UI for these meal bookings? Discuss first!"

Intent: build the Angular front-end UI for the already-implemented canteen meal-booking backend APIs, with discussion before implementation. The existing mobile app consumes the same APIs; a web FE is additionally required.

After a discussion phase and an `AskUserQuestion` block, the user selected:
- **Scope** (multi-select, all three chosen): Employee Meal Booking screen, Admin bookings register, Kitchen headcount dashboard.
- **Planner API**: Add a `GetMealPlanner` endpoint (server owns menu/rate/cutoff resolution) rather than composing on the front end.
- **Book request**: Extend `BookMealsRequest` with `items[]` rather than grouping client-side.
- **Layout**: Week grid (day columns × meal-session rows) with a selected ASCII preview showing a `Book 4 meals · ₹110` action bar.

The user then interrupted with an additional constraint:
> "Please make it as mobile friendly as possible!"

And finally confirmed sequencing:
> "No start with backend like you originally said. Then UI! Thanks"

Security/operational constraints in force (from stored memory, stated as project rules):
- **"User runs builds, not Claude — never run dotnet build/test or ng build here; say what went unverified instead."** This was honoured throughout; no build or test command was executed.
- HRMS keeps DB migrations in two unconnected folders (`HRMS_Payroll/SolutionOneWeb/App_Data/DbMigrations/NNN_*.sql` and `HRMS_BackEnd/SolutionOne_DataAccessLayer/SqlScripts/Migration_<Thing>_<yyyyMMdd>.sql`); SolutionOneWeb ports need a backend `SqlScripts` counterpart or EF throws "Invalid column name".
- "script 035/036" references in backend comments actually mean SolutionOneWeb scripts 239/240.

Environment note: the session runs in "auto mode", which instructs doing work through the Bash tool (cat/sed/grep/heredocs/python) rather than the dedicated Read/Edit/Write tools where Bash can do the job.

## 2. Key Technical Concepts

- **Backend**: .NET (C#), layered solution — `SolutionOne_Core` (models), `SolutionOne_DataAccessLayer` (EF Core repositories + entities + `SqlScripts`), `SolutionOne_BusinessLogicLayer` (services), `SolutionOneWebPortal` (API controllers), `SolutionOne_Tests` (xUnit + Moq).
- **EF Core** with `HrmsystemContext`; `DateOnly`/`TimeOnly` column types; filtered unique index `UX_HR_CMS_MealBooking_ActiveMeal`; SQL error numbers 2601/2627 for duplicate-key detection.
- **RBAC**: `HR_MenuItems` (route-keyed), `HR_MenuActions`, `HR_RolePermissions`, `HR_UserScreenAccess`; `[Permission(Modules.X, Actions.Y)]` controller attribute; permissions cached 5 minutes.
- **Canteen domain**: `HR_CMS_MealSession` (with `OrderCutoffTime` + `OrderCutoffDaysBefore`), `HR_CMS_Config` (single row, `MaxOrderCutoffDaysBefore`), `HR_CMS_MenuPlan` (PlanDate + MealTypeId = MSessionId + ItemId), `HR_CMS_ItemMaster`, `HR_CMS_MealBooking`, `HR_CMS_MenuPublish`.
- **`MealOrderCutoff`** (in `SolutionOne_Core`): the single place that both states and computes the ordering deadline — `LocalDeadline`, `Describe`, `DescribeFor`, `DayLabel`, `FormatTime`. Deadlines are evaluated in the **canteen's** time zone (branch → company → `DefaultTimeZoneId`), never the client's.
- **`CanteenMealRates`** (internal static, BLL): resolves Daily vs Adhoc shares; `FacilityNotEnabledMessage`.
- **`TimeZoneLookup`** (`SolutionOne_Core.Utilities`): `Find`, `FromUtc`, `ToUtc`.
- **Frontend**: Angular 20.3, standalone components, module-per-feature with `loadChildren`, `@if`/`@for`/`@else if (x; as y)` control-flow blocks, `strict: true` + `strictTemplates: true` + `noPropertyAccessFromIndexSignature: true`.
- **DevExtreme 26.1** (`devextreme-angular`) is the UI library — `DxButtonModule`, `DxSelectBoxModule`, `DxDateBoxModule`, `DxTextBoxModule`, `DxDataGrid` via `CommonGridComponent`. No calendar/scheduler component is used anywhere in the app.
- **App shell**: `LayoutService` publishes `app-mobile` / `app-tablet` / `app-nav-open` classes on `<body>`; breakpoints `(max-width: 767.98px)` mobile, `(min-width: 768px) and (max-width: 1023.98px)` tablet. Only `sidenav.component.scss` consumes them today; module screens use Bootstrap 5 grid classes + media queries.
- **Design tokens** in `src/styles.scss` (`--page-bg`, `--card-bg`, `--card-border`, `--accent: #ff6600`, `--accent-soft`, `--text-main/secondary/soft/muted`, `--page-content-max-width: 1400px`, etc.). Global classes: `.page-wrapper`, `.form-card`, `.form-card-header`, `.form-card-header-icon/-left/-text`, `.form-card-title`, `.form-card-subtitle`, `.form-card-body`, `.form-card-footer`, `.section-card`, `.section-header`, `.header-title`, `.section-body`. **No dark theme** in this app. **No global `.visually-hidden`** utility (defined per-component).
- **`IMPLEMENTED_ROUTES`** (`layout/sidenav/implemented-routes.ts`): the sidebar renders a `HR_MenuItems` row only if its route is listed here. "THIS IS NOT AUTHORIZATION."
