No summary of the completed work had yet been delivered to the user.

## 9. Optional Next Step

Write the completion report to the user. The user's last instruction was:

> "No start with backend like you originally said. Then UI! Thanks"

Both halves are now written, so the next step is to report — not to start new work. The report should cover: the four backend endpoints and the additive `items[]` change; the RBAC migration `Migration_CanteenAdminScreens_20261024.sql` with the reminder to **edit `@RoleCodes` before running it** (it defaults to `ADMIN` only); the run order SQL → API → front end; the three screens and how each behaves at phone width; and — per the standing project rule, "never run dotnet build/test or ng build here; say what went unverified instead" — an explicit statement that **nothing has been compiled or type-checked**: `dotnet build`, `dotnet test` (including the 8 new tests in `MealBookingServiceTests.cs`) and `ng build` are all still to be run by the user. It should also name the two deliberate limitations: the Bookings Register shows at most 500 rows per call with a visible warning when the range exceeds that, and `CanteenDashboard/Summary` still counts menu-publish recipients rather than meals.

